<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Basis continues to soften.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Basis continues to soften.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis offers for soybean meal continued to soften Monday as the recent rise in prices prompted feed mixers to look for substitutes, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Prices have gotten so high they (feed mixers) are taking soymeal out of the formula,&quot; a broker said.</p>
<p>Brokers said they were looking for a further decline in the NOPA crush this week after last week's drop to 29.97 million bushels from 30.86 million a week earlier. NOPA is due to issue weekly data on Thursday.</p>
<p>Cottonseed meal was among the commodities said to be gaining market share at the expense of soybean meal.  </p>
